  "title": "Consciousness as subjective experience",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "88ecfeeb-d4fe-4bb4-a511-52d7d58000f3",
      "text": "Consciousness, roughly equivalent to sentience, is subjective experience: a being is conscious if there is something it is like to be it. Its dimensions include sensory, affective, cognitive and agentive experience, and self-consciousness. Chalmers assumes that consciousness is real and not an illusion.",
